  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shiv Shankar Prasad Sahu vs The State Of Bihar on 18 October, 2016 Author: Rajendra Kumar Mishra Bench: Rajendra Kumar Mishra In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.43651 of 2016 Arising Out of PS.Case No. -11 Year- 2013 Thana -Government Official C Muzaffarpur ====================================================== Shiv Shankar Prasad Sahu, Son of late Asharfi Lal Sahu, Resident of Village- Tinpkhariya Malighat, P.S- Mithanpura, District Muzaffarpur. .... .. Versus The State of Bihar .... .... Opposite Party = = = = = = = ==== == == == == = Appearance : For the Petitioner/s : Mr. Bela Singh For the Opposite Party/s : Smt. Sucheta Yadav ===================================================== = Coram: Honourable Mr. Justice Rajendra Kumar Mishra Oral Order 2 18-10-2016",
    "facts": "The petitioner apprehends his arrest in connection with C Case No. 11 of 2013, registered under Sections 59(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, pending in the court of the 3rd Additional Sessions Judge-cum-Special Judge, Muzaffapur. The accusation is that on 13.11.2011 Food Safety Officer purchased Atta/Flour from the Mill of the petitioner and on test the same was found adulterated and insects were found in the said flour.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that while Atta was purchased on 13.11.2011 and the same was tested on 26.11.2011 and as such it is natural to grow insects in the flour/atta after 13 days.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that while Atta was purchased on 13.11.2011 and the same was tested on 26.11.2011 and as such it is natural to grow insects in the flour/atta after 13 days.",
